 "result_text": "`idna.decode(b'\\x8d\\xd2')` now raises `idna.IDNAError(\"Invalid ASCII in A-label\")` instead of `UnicodeDecodeError`. I haven't run the repo's test suite. I only ran a quick check on three inputs, and all three raised `IDNAError`: the issue's bytes, `b'xn--\\xff'` and `b'xn--a-'`.\n\nAll three changes are in `idna/core.py`:\n- **`decode()` and `encode()`:** both decoded byte input as ASCII with no error handling, so both now catch the failure and raise `IDNAError`. The issue only reported `decode()`, but `encode()` had the same crash.\n- **`ulabel()` Punycode step:** I wrapped the Punycode decode so a malformed A-label also raises `IDNAError` instead of a bare `UnicodeError`.\n- **`ulabel()` trailing-hyphen check:** I replaced the ASCII-decode-and-index check with a plain byte comparison. The old version could raise `UnicodeDecodeError` on non-ASCII bytes.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
